==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{term|aprender|lang=roa-opt}}, from {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|apprendere|lang=la}}, alternative form of {{term|apprehendere|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|apprehendō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/ɐ.pɾẽ.ˈdeɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|a|pren|der|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|aprend|er}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to [[learn]], to acquire [[knowledge]]
#: ''Em dois anos, '''aprendi''' francês.'' — “In two years, I learned French.”
# {{context|intransitive|lang=pt}} to be able to [[learn]]
#: ''Meu filho caçula '''aprende''' mais rápido que o irmão.'' — “My youngest son learns faster than his brother.”
# {{pt-verb form of|aprender|ar|subjunctive|future|singular|first}}
# {{pt-verb form of|aprender|ar|subjunctive|future|singular|third}}
# {{pt-verb form of|aprender|ar|personal infinitive||singular|first}}
# {{pt-verb form of|aprender|ar|personal infinitive||singular|third}}

